hadiths[41]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1197","It is narrated from Nafi‘ (may Allah have mercy on him) that ‘Abdullah ibn ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) sent him to ask ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) whether a man can have intercourse with his wife during her menstruation. She replied: “(The wife) should tie a waist-wrapper tightly around her lower part, then if he (the husband) wishes, he may have intercourse with her.”"
"1198","It is narrated from Khuzaymah bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man asked the Prophet (ﷺ) about having intercourse with women from behind, or about a man having intercourse with his wife in her anus (Imam Shafi’i, may Allah have mercy on him, was unsure about the wording). The Prophet (ﷺ) said: “It is permissible.” When the man turned back, the Prophet (ﷺ) called him or ordered that he be brought back, and asked him: “What did you say? In which of the two private parts? From behind in the front private part? If it is like that, then it is correct. Or from behind in the anus itself? If that is what is meant, then it is not permissible. Indeed, Allah does not shy away from the truth. Do not approach women in their anus.” Imam Shafi’i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: They asked, “What do you say about this chain of narration?” So I said: My uncle and Abdullah bin Ali bin al-Sa’ib are both trustworthy. And he said: Muhammad (may Allah have mercy on him) informed me about the hadith scholar Ansari, that he spoke well about him, and Khuzaymah is among those narrators whose trustworthiness no scholar doubts. Therefore, I do not consider intercourse with women in the anus to be permissible; rather, I prohibit it."
"1199","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""What is the matter with people that they have intercourse with their slave women and then practice coitus interruptus (withdrawal)? Now, if any slave woman comes to me and her master admits to having had intercourse with her, I will attribute the (child) to his father. After that, whether you practice coitus interruptus or not, it is up to you."
"1200","From another chain, through Safiyyah bint Abi Ubaid, a narration similar to Salim's hadith is reported from Umar (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"1201","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The child belongs to the (owner of the) bed, and for the adulterer there are stones."
"1202","Narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that Abd bin Zam‘ah and Sa‘d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with them both) brought the case of the son of Zam‘ah’s slave woman to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Sa‘d said: “O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! My brother had made a will that when you go to Makkah, look at the child of Zam‘ah’s slave woman and take him, for he is my son.” Abdullah bin Zam‘ah said: “He is my brother and the son of my father’s slave woman, and he was born on my father’s bed.” The Prophet ﷺ saw that the boy clearly resembled ‘Utbah, then said: “O Abdullah bin Zam‘ah! He will go with you, for the child belongs to the (owner of the) bed. (And he ordered Umm al-Mu’minin Sawdah, may Allah be pleased with her): O Sawdah! Observe veil from him.”"
"1203","Abdullah bin Abi Yazid narrated from his father who said that Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) sent a man to an old man from Banu Zuhrah who lived among our houses. I also went with him to Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), and he asked him about the birth of children in the pre-Islamic period. He said: ""The bed would belong to one person and the semen to another (that is, the owner of the bed and the owner of the semen would be different)."" Upon this, Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""You have spoken the truth, but the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) has decided in favor of the owner of the bed."
"1204","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man from among the villagers came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: ""My wife has given birth to a black child."" The Prophet ﷺ asked him: ""Do you have any camels?"" He said: ""Yes."" The Prophet ﷺ asked: ""What are their colors?"" He said: ""Red."" The Prophet ﷺ asked: ""Is there among them any that is white with a tinge of black?"" He said: ""Yes."" The Prophet ﷺ asked: ""What do you think, where did that come from?"" He said: ""Some lineage must have drawn it out."" The Prophet ﷺ said: ""Perhaps this (child) has also been drawn out by some distant lineage."" (Meaning, due to resemblance with a distant relative, the child's color has become black.)"
"1205","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man from the tribe of Banu Fazara came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said, ""My wife has given birth to a dark-skinned child."" The Prophet (ﷺ) asked, ""Do you have any camels?"" He said, ""Yes."" The Prophet (ﷺ) asked, ""What are their colors?"" He said, ""They are red."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Are there any among them that are dusky white?"" He said, ""Yes, there are some that are dusky white."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Where did they come from?"" He said, ""Perhaps some lineage has brought it out."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Perhaps this (child) has also been brought out by some lineage."
"1206","Ubaid bin Umair narrated that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! My wife does not prevent the hand of any toucher."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Divorce her."" He said, ""I love her (I cannot divorce her)."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Then keep her."
"1207","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from coming to the mosques of Allah, and when they go out (for the mosques), they should go out without applying perfume."
"1208","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from coming to the mosques of Allah."
"1209","Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that Hind (may Allah be pleased with her) came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: ""O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! Abu Sufyan (my husband) is a miserly man. He does not give me enough expenses which are sufficient for me and my children. If I take something from his wealth without his knowledge, will there be any sin upon me?"" The Prophet ﷺ said: ""You may take in a good manner what is sufficient for you and your children."
"1210","It is narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that Hind bint Utbah (may Allah be pleased with her) came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! Abu Sufyan is a miserly man and I only have that much expenditure which he gives me (which is insufficient)."" So the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Take from his wealth, according to what is customary, enough for you and your children."
"1211","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I have one dinar."" He (peace be upon him) said: ""Spend it on yourself."" He said: ""I have another."" He (peace be upon him) said: ""Spend it on your child."" He said: ""I have another."" He (peace be upon him) said: ""Spend it on your family."" He said: ""I have another."" He (peace be upon him) said: ""Spend it on your servant."" He said: ""I have another."" He (peace be upon him) said: ""You know best where to spend it."" Sa‘id said that when Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated this hadith, he would say: ""Your son says, 'Spend on me or entrust me to someone else.' Your wife says, 'Spend on me or divorce me.' And your servant says, 'Spend on me or sell me.'"
"1212","It is narrated from Abu Al-Zinad, he says: I asked Sa'id bin Al-Musayyib about a man who does not have wealth to spend on his wife, so he said: ""Separation will be made between them."" Abu Al-Zinad asked: ""Is this Sunnah?"" Sa'id said: ""Yes, it is Sunnah."" Imam Shafi'i, may Allah have mercy on him, said: Sa'id's statement that it is Sunnah indicates that it is the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him."
"1213","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote letters to the commanders of the armies regarding those men who are absent (from home) and not with their wives. He ordered them to hold such men accountable, that they should either provide maintenance to their wives or divorce them. And if they divorce them, then they should also give the maintenance for the period during which they did not provide for them."
"1214","It is narrated from Muhammad bin Munkadir that a man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: ""I have wealth and I have children, and my father also has wealth, but he wants to take from my wealth to feed his (other) children."" Upon this, the Prophet ﷺ said: ""You and your wealth belong to your father."
"1215","It is narrated from Sa'id bin al-Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him) that the daughter of Muhammad bin Maslamah was married to Rafi' bin Khadij (may Allah be pleased with him). Due to old age or some other reason, he began to dislike her. When he intended to divorce her, his wife said: ""Do not divorce me, keep me with you and decide about my turn as you wish."" Then Allah Almighty revealed this verse: ""And if a woman fears indifference from her husband..."" __QUR_N__"
"1216","Ibn Abi Mulaika narrates that Aqil bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) married Fatimah bint Utbah. Fatimah said to him: ""You stay with me and I will spend on you."" Whenever he would come to her, she (Fatimah) would say: ""Where are Utbah and Shaybah?"" Upon hearing this, he would remain silent. One day, he entered the house feeling annoyed, and Fatimah said: ""Where are Utbah bin Rabi'ah and Shaybah bin Rabi'ah?"" Aqil (may Allah be pleased with him) angrily said: ""When you enter Hell, they will be on your left side."" (This statement was very hard on her) so she tied her clothes and went to Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) and related the whole matter to him. Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) sent Ibn Abbas and Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with them both) (to decide the matter). Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: ""I will surely separate them,"" and Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""I will not allow separation between the two elders of Banu Abd Manaf."" Ibn Abi Mulaika said that when both of them came to him, they found him extremely angry, then both of them reconciled between them."
"1217","It is narrated from Ubaidah (may Allah have mercy on him) regarding this verse: ""If you fear a breach between them (the husband and wife), appoint two arbiters, one from his family and the other from hers"" (An-Nisa: 35), that during the caliphate of Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), a husband and wife came to him along with people from their respective families. Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) ordered them to appoint one arbiter from the man's family and one from the woman's family. Then he (may Allah be pleased with him) said to the two arbiters: ""Do you know what your task is? If you deem it appropriate, reconcile them, and if you wish, separate them."" Upon hearing this, the woman said: ""I am content with the decision of Allah's Book, whether it is reconciliation or separation,"" and the man said: ""I do not accept separation."" At this, Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""By Allah, you are lying; you must accept both options in the same way."
"1218","Saeed bin Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated that the daughter of Muhammad bin Maslamah was married to Rafi’ bin Khadij (may Allah be pleased with him). Due to old age or some other reason, he began to dislike her, to the extent that he intended to divorce her. Then she said: ""Do not divorce me; I forgo my rights."" Upon this, the verse was revealed: ""And if a woman fears from her husband contempt or evasion..."" (__QUR_N__: An-Nisa: 128). He said: Then this practice became established."
"1219","Iyas bin Abdullah bin Abu Dhabab reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Do not beat Allah's female servants."" Then Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: ""O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! Women have become bold towards their husbands."" So the Prophet ﷺ allowed them to be beaten. Then many women came to the house of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and complained about their husbands. The Prophet ﷺ said: ""Seventy women have come to the house of Muhammad ﷺ complaining about their husbands. Beware! Such people are not good."
"1220","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) gave a boy the choice to select either his father or his mother."
"1221","Yunus bin Abdullah Al-Jarmi narrated that Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) gave me the choice to choose between my mother and my uncle, then regarding my younger brother he said: ""He would also have the same choice if he had reached his (i.e., my) age."
"1222","It is narrated from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) through the chain of Yunus, from ‘Ammarah, similarly, and in this hadith it is stated: ""At that time, I was seven or eight years old."
"1223","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he said: ""The one who takes an oath of *ila* is he who swears never to approach his wife forever."
"1224","It is narrated from Sulaiman bin Yasar (may Allah have mercy on him) that I saw more than ten companions of the Prophet ﷺ who would stop a person who had taken an oath of abstinence (ila) and ask him (to either reconcile or divorce). Imam Shafi’i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The minimum number for (bidh’atu ‘ashar) is thirteen, and he also said that they were the Ansar companions (may Allah be pleased with them)."
"1225","It is narrated from Sulaiman bin Yasar, may Allah have mercy on him, that he stated: I found more than ten companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, all of them would make the one who took an oath of abstinence stand and ask him (about divorce or reconciliation)."
"1226","Amr bin Salamah narrated that I was present with Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), and he made the one who had taken an oath of abstinence stand (for a decision), so that he would either divorce (his wife) or take her back."
"1227","It is narrated from Marwan bin Hakam that Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) made the one who took an oath of abstinence stand (so that a decision could be made)."
"1228","It is narrated from Tawus that Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) used to make the one who performed ila stand and ask him about (divorce or reconciliation)."
"1229","Qasim bin Muhammad (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated that when Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) heard mention of a man who swore an oath that he would not go to his wife, and then left her for five months, she did not consider this correct unless he was stopped and a decision was made. She used to say: ""Allah the Exalted has said that either keep (her) in a good manner or release (her) in a good way."
"1230","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: ""When a man makes an oath of abstinence (ila) from his wife, divorce does not take place, even if four months pass, until he is made to stand (before the judge) so that he either divorces her or takes her back."
"1231","Ja'far bin Muhammad narrated from his father that Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) used to make the one who took an oath of abstinence stand."
"1232","It is narrated from Umrah that she informed that Habibah bint Sahl (may Allah be pleased with her) told her that she was married to Thabit bin Qais bin Shamas. And when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out for the morning prayer, he found Habibah bint Sahl at his door in the darkness. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, upon seeing her, asked: ""Who is this?"" She said: ""I am Habibah bint Sahl, O Messenger of Allah!"" He ﷺ asked: ""What troubles you?"" She said: ""I and Thabit cannot live together."" Then when Thabit bin Qais (may Allah be pleased with him) came, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: ""This is Habibah bint Sahl, regarding whom Allah has willed, you have spoken."" Habibah said: ""O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! Whatever he gave me (as dowry) is with me."" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Thabit: ""Take (the dowry) from her."" He took it back, and Habibah (may Allah be pleased with her) returned to her family after obtaining khul‘."
"1233","It is narrated from Habibah bint Sahl (may Allah be pleased with her) that she came to the Prophet (ﷺ) in the dark, and complained with her hands about something, saying: ""I and Thabit bin Qais (may Allah be pleased with him) cannot live together."" Habibah says: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to Thabit: ""O Thabit, take back the dowry you gave her."" He took back the dowry, and she sat after obtaining khul‘ (divorce)."
"1234","Nafi' narrated regarding the freed slave woman of Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd that she obtained khul' from her husband by giving him everything she had, and Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) did not object to this."
"1235","It is narrated from Umm Bakrah Al-Aslamiyyah that she took khul‘ from her husband Abdullah bin Asid, then both of them brought this matter to ‘Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: ""If you have mentioned something else, then it is what has been mentioned; if not, then it is a divorce."
"1236","It is narrated from Ata that Ibn Abbas and Ibn al-Zubair (may Allah be pleased with them) said regarding a woman who has taken khul‘ and then her husband divorces her: ""She does not need a divorce, because the husband has divorced one who is no longer his wife."
"1237","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas and Ibn Zubair (may Allah be pleased with them both) that they said: ""A woman who has obtained khula should not be divorced during her waiting period, because now the husband has divorced her and she is no longer his wife."
